course: dictionary
lesson: 13879
title: A Scottish word: kirk
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one country. Kirk is a Scottish word for church. When you read «the village kirk», you can picture a church in a Scottish village, and the word also tells you the story is probably set in Scotland or northern England.
explain: Look at the words around kirk to check its meaning. «The village kirk rang its bell for the Sunday service.» A bell and a service are things you find at a church, so kirk must mean church. Swap church into the sentence. It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: Kirk can also be a name. In «Captain Kirk», Kirk is a person's name, not a building. A capital letter can help too: the Kirk, with a capital K, means the Church of Scotland, which is the main church in Scotland.
fact: Kirk means church, and it is a Scottish word.
fact: A small k, as in «the kirk», means a church building.
fact: A capital K, as in «the Kirk», means the Church of Scotland, the main Presbyterian church there.
fact: Kirk is also a first name or surname, as in «Captain Kirk» from Star Trek.
fact: Some Scottish place names, such as «Kirkcaldy» and «Falkirk», contain the word kirk, which is a clue that the place is in Scotland.
exercise: «The villagers walked to the kirk every Sunday morning.» What is a kirk? | *A church | A shop | A kind of boat
exercise: Grandad says, «The Kirk is the main church in Scotland.» What is the Kirk? | A kind of Scottish dinner | A road in London | *The Church of Scotland
exercise: In «Captain Kirk walked onto the bridge of the ship», what kind of word is Kirk? | *A name | A kind of sweet | A town in Scotland | A church
test: Which word in «the village kirk rang its bell» means church? | rang | bell | village | *kirk
test: Why does a capital K in «the Kirk» matter? | *It names the Church of Scotland | It means the word is a first name | It means the church is very small | It shows the sentence is a question
exam: Which sentence uses kirk as a name? | «Ella walked past the kirk on her way home.» | «The kirk bell rang across the village.» | «The kirk was full for the wedding.» | *«Captain Kirk led the crew of the Enterprise.»
